    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problems—something I’ve always found both intimidating and fascinating. My parents taught me early that numbers had meaning beyond just calculations, but my low conscientiousness makes problem-solving feel like a puzzle I sometimes struggle to fit together neatly. Still, I enjoy the logic behind equations, even if I prefer visualizing concepts through art or music instead of pure computation.",
